## SQ-NDM-01 | Nether's Delight member: one mod, mixin applies
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -n "nethersdelight" logs/latest.log \| grep -i "error\|exception\|mixin\|duplicate" \| head`; mod list / `creativedelight_members.txt`
@pass one `nethersdelight` mod, version `1.19-3.1-ce-19.2-01`, display name "Nether's Delight (Creative Delight)"; `nethersdelight.ce.mixins.json` applies `FungusColonyRulesMixin` with no error; no duplicate-mod crash
@fails duplicate id: the 3.1 jar still in `mods/` or `server_mods/`; mixin error: the `m_213897_` constant or the class changed
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] members: \[.*\bnethersdelight\b
bootreject (?i)nethersdelight.*(duplicate|mixin.*(error|fail)|exception)
bootreject (?i)duplicate mods? .*nethersdelight
shell ! ls mods | grep -i "^NethersDelight-1.19-3.1"
shell grep -hE "nethersdelight.ce.mixins|FungusColonyRulesMixin|nethersdelight.*1.19-3.1-ce" logs/latest.log logs/debug.log 2>/dev/null | head -8; true
look rows/SQ-NDM-01.shell.txt: version 1.19-3.1-ce-19.2-01 and the mixin config listed; the display name "Nether's Delight (Creative Delight)" is a client mod-list check

## SQ-NDM-02 | Mimicarnation in a flower pot (pot at 256)
@group A
@commands `/setblock ~ ~ ~ minecraft:flower_pot`; bot uses `nethersdelight:mimicarnation` on it; check block state; bot uses empty hand on it; plant it again, then break it
@pass pot becomes `nethersdelight:potted_mimicarnation`; empty hand gives the Mimicarnation back and leaves `minecraft:flower_pot`; breaking drops a Flower Pot and a Mimicarnation
@fails no block: the `RegisterEvent` subscriber did not run; planting refused: `addPlant` missing (common setup)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb passed
> forceload add 250 495 300 510
> setblock 256 -60 500 minecraft:flower_pot
> pbot spawn ndm2 256 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot hold ndm2 nethersdelight:mimicarnation
> pbot use ndm2 256 -60 500 up
> execute if block 256 -60 500 nethersdelight:potted_mimicarnation run say NDM02 potted
> pbot hold ndm2 minecraft:air
> pbot use ndm2 256 -60 500 up
> execute if block 256 -60 500 minecraft:flower_pot run say NDM02 empty pot back
> clear ndm2 nethersdelight:mimicarnation 0
> pbot hold ndm2 nethersdelight:mimicarnation
> pbot use ndm2 256 -60 500 up
> cdevtest break 256 -60 500
expect NDM02 potted
expect NDM02 empty pot back
expect Found 1 matching item
expect verb=break .*broken=true before="?nethersdelight:potted_mimicarnation
expect verb=break drops=\S*minecraft:flower_pot:1\b
expect verb=break drops=\S*nethersdelight:mimicarnation:1\b
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
> pbot remove ndm2

## SQ-NDM-03 | potted mimicarnation and meal_item tags
@group A
@commands `/dumptags` block `minecraft:flower_pots`, item `nethersdelight:meal_item`
@pass flower_pots holds `nethersdelight:potted_mimicarnation`; meal_item holds `farmersdelight:stuffed_potato`
@fails CD `nethersdelight/tags.js` not in the jar, or `global.CD.on('nethersdelight')` false
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb passed
> cdevtest tag block minecraft:flower_pots
> cdevtest tag item nethersdelight:meal_item
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=minecraft:flower_pots .*nethersdelight:potted_mimicarnation(,|$)
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=nethersdelight:meal_item .*farmersdelight:stuffed_potato(,|$)
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-NDM-04 | Stuffed Hoglin and netherite machete ids; the pot cooks it (pot at 295)
@group A
@commands Recipe lookup by id: `farmersdelight:cooking/stuffed_hoglin`, `minecraft:netherite_machete_smithing`, `nethersdelight:cooking/stuffed_hoglin`, `nethersdelight:netherite_machete_smithing`; bot cooks Stuffed Hoglin in a heated Cooking Pot (2 Nether Salad, Raw Stuffed Hoglin)
@pass the first two exist (Cooking Pot; smithing table: Diamond Machete + Netherite Ingot), the old two do not; the pot gives Stuffed Hoglin
@fails old ids present: `replaced_resources` not applied
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
> cdevtest rdetail stuffed_hoglin
> cdevtest rdetail netherite_machete_smithing
expect verb=rdetail id=farmersdelight:cooking/stuffed_hoglin serializer=
expect verb=rdetail id=minecraft:netherite_machete_smithing serializer=
reject verb=rdetail id=nethersdelight:cooking/stuffed_hoglin serializer=
reject verb=rdetail id=nethersdelight:netherite_machete_smithing serializer=
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
> setblock 295 -60 500 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 295 -59 500 farmersdelight:cooking_pot
> data merge block 295 -59 500 {Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"farmersdelight:nether_salad",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"farmersdelight:nether_salad",Count:1b},{Slot:2b,id:"nethersdelight:raw_stuffed_hoglin",Count:1b}]}}
> cdevtest tickwarp 500
waitlog verb=tickwarp end= 60
> data get block 295 -59 500 Inventory
expect Slot: [68]b?, id: "nethersdelight:stuffed_hoglin"
look rdetail: the pot recipe's inputs and the smithing table Diamond Machete + Netherite Ingot

## SQ-NDM-05 | fungus colony survival on dirt by daylight (262 open, 268 boxed, 274 rich soul soil)
@group A
@commands `/time set noon`; `/setblock` dirt, then `nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony` on it under open sky, then `/setblock` a block beside it; repeat under a 3-block roof in the dark; repeat on `nethersdelight:rich_soul_soil` in daylight; bot tries to place a colony item on dirt at noon
@pass open-sky colony on dirt breaks on the neighbor update (drops the item); the roofed one and the rich soul soil one stay; placing on dirt in daylight is refused
@fails survive check not merged (mixin)
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
> time set noon
> setblock 262 -60 500 minecraft:dirt
> setblock 262 -59 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony
> setblock 263 -59 500 minecraft:stone
> execute unless block 262 -59 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony run say NDM05 open-sky colony broke
> fill 266 -60 498 270 -57 502 minecraft:stone hollow
> setblock 268 -59 500 minecraft:dirt
> setblock 268 -58 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony
> setblock 269 -58 500 minecraft:stone
> execute if block 268 -58 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony run say NDM05 roofed colony stays
> setblock 274 -61 500 nethersdelight:rich_soul_soil
> setblock 274 -60 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony
> setblock 275 -60 500 minecraft:stone
> execute if block 274 -60 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony run say NDM05 rich soul soil colony stays
> setblock 278 -61 500 minecraft:dirt
> pbot spawn ndm5 278 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot hold ndm5 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony
> pbot use ndm5 278 -61 500 up
> execute unless block 278 -60 500 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony run say NDM05 placing on dirt in daylight refused
expect NDM05 open-sky colony broke
expect NDM05 roofed colony stays
expect NDM05 rich soul soil colony stays
expect NDM05 placing on dirt in daylight refused
> pbot remove ndm5
look the broken open-sky colony dropped its item (an item entity at 262 -59 500)

## SQ-NDM-06 | 50 colonies on rich soul soil grow with random ticks (bot near them, x 280..289)
@group A
@commands 50 colonies at age 0 on rich soul soil, `/gamerule randomTickSpeed 30`, wait 1200 ticks; `grep -i "fungus\|colony\|CropGrow" logs/latest.log`
@pass colonies reach age 3; no errors; Calendar's crop-grow hook still runs (season type nether, no penalty)
@fails growth stuck: Calendar event refused, check CropSeasons type for the colonies
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
> fill 280 -61 500 289 -61 504 nethersdelight:rich_soul_soil
> fill 280 -60 500 289 -60 504 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony[age=0]
> pbot spawn ndm6 285 -60 507 minecraft:overworld survival
> cdevtest randomtick 280 -60 500 289 -60 504 9
> cdevtest ages 280 -60 500 289 -60 504 nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony
> pbot remove ndm6
expect verb=ages block=nethersdelight:crimson_fungus_colony prop=age n=50 mean=[1-3]\.
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
reject (?i)(fungus|colony|CropGrow).*(error|exception)
look the histogram reaches age 3 (season type nether: no growth penalty; 9 random ticks per block = the old 1200 ticks at randomTickSpeed 30)

